      "message": "Having thought about this: why do we even allow  the setvar() called from this code trigger a compaction? \n\nWhy not call compaction first and then just fill the rest of the last page with erased values?\n\nIf we care about the wasted space in the last page we can call compaction again. This could take a bit longer time, (which does not matter much when `tpm_erase_objects()` is invoked) but would result in a much simpler code.",
